(*"experience_schema.acyclic_experience_relationship"
The **acyclic_experience_relationship** function determines whether the graph of instances of the entity data type <<express:experience_schema.experience,experience>> that contains relation as one of its links contains a cycle. This function may be used to evaluate either an <<express:experience_schema.experience_relationship,experience_relationship>> or any of its subtypes.

The function returns TRUE if no cycle has been detected. Otherwise it returns FALSE.
*)


(*"experience_schema.acyclic_experience_relationship.__note"
The algorithm of the function is explained in annex E.2.
*)

(*"experience_schema.acyclic_experience_relationship.__note"
This function is not used in this schema. It is defined here because other ISO 10303 integrated resources and application protocols that use the <<express:experience_schema.experience_relationship,experience_relationship>> entity include rules that use this function.
*)

(*"experience_schema.acyclic_experience_relationship.relation"
(input) the candidate <<express:experience_schema.experience_relationship,experience_relationship>> to be checked.
*)


(*"experience_schema.acyclic_experience_relationship.relatives"
(input) the set of instances of the entity data type <<express:experience_schema.experience,experience>> that the function is searching for in the <<express:experience_schema.experience_relationship.relating_experience,relating_experience>> parameter of the **relation** argument.
*)


(*"experience_schema.acyclic_experience_relationship.specific_relation"
(input) the fully qualified name of a subtype of the <<express:experience_schema.experience_relationship,experience_relationship>> entity.
*)


(*"experience_schema.acyclic_experience_type_relationship"
The **acyclic_experience_type_relationship** function determines whether the graph of instances of the entity data type <<express:experience_schema.experience_type,experience_type>> that contains relation as one of its links contains a cycle. This function may be used to evaluate either an <<express:experience_schema.experience_type_relationship,experience_type_relationship>> or any of its subtypes.

The function returns TRUE if no cycle has been detected. Otherwise it returns FALSE.
*)


(*"experience_schema.acyclic_experience_type_relationship.__note"
The algorithm of the function is explained in annex E.2.
*)

